From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: show GL frames on the display's refresh

The guest's vblank timer runs at the Mac display's rate (the EDID carries
it) but at its own phase. Shown as soon as the GPU finished them, two
guest frames sometimes landed in one refresh of the Mac and none in the
next: at a steady 120 frames a second from the guest only 107-109 distinct
frames a second reached the 120 Hz MacBook panel (ScreenCaptureKit count,
bench lock), 15-20 % of frames were never seen and 5-10 % of refreshes
repeated one. The guest looked smooth from the inside (Chrome's rAF:
120.01 fps, p99 8.4 ms) and juddered on the Mac.

Finished frames now wait in a short queue (a jitter buffer, at most three)
and once per refresh, 3 ms before the vsync, the oldest one is put on the
layer. A display link on the window's screen (on a thread of its own: the
main thread ran ticks milliseconds late now and then) times it; ProMotion
is asked for the panel's full rate. A frame that comes less than half a
refresh after the previous one replaces it; frames left over at every
tick for a quarter second are trimmed one at a time, so the queue never
holds more delay than the guest's timing needs. The link pauses after 30
idle refreshes. Five present surfaces instead of three: one on screen, one
committed but not latched yet, up to three queued.

Result on the MacBook (120 Hz, bench lock, 12 s of a 120 fps page, three
runs): 119.2-120.0 distinct frames a second on screen, 98.3-99.8 % of guest
frames shown exactly once (gpu-native: 108-110, 74-82 %); QEMU flush to
screen 10-14 ms median (gpu-native 5-7 ms), one refresh more. glmark2
quick, 8 runs each: median 2764 vs 2829 (-2 %, within the run-to-run
spread of 2387-2972).

OMACVM_GL_VSYNC=0 goes back to showing frames when drawn.
OMACVM_GL_LEAD_MS sets how long before the vsync a frame goes on the layer.
OMACVM_GL_FPS=1 logs ticks, frames shown, repeats, merged and dropped
frames and draws without a free surface once a second.

Upstream: not sent (depends on the IOSurface present, an OmacVM patch).
Tests: scratchpad tools for now (pacing page + ScreenCaptureKit counter,
see docs/architecture/graphics.md, frame pacing); glmark2 quick for
throughput. Applies after qemu-cocoa-gl-present-iosurface.patch.

